{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund follow-up support for adults diagnosed with autism or ADHD later in life",
        "additional_details": "Many adults wait years for an assessment, then are discharged with a report and a list of websites. Those diagnosed in their 40s, 50s and beyond have spent decades being called lazy or difficult.\r\nWithout follow-up, many are left alone with grief, burnout and no route to help with work, money or mental health. A follow-up appointment, a named contact and signposting to workplace adjustments, benefits advice and peer support would turn a label into real help.",
        "background": "We want the Government to fund at least one follow-up appointment and a named point of contact for every adult diagnosed with autism or ADHD, so a diagnosis comes with a plan, not just a report.",
